%% REWRITTEN: previous version documented an opt-in "Lovable AI Gateway" fallback that does
%% not exist in current code. /api/chat now returns a plain error when the Python backend is
%% unreachable or fails; there is no cloud-model fallback path today.
flowchart TD
  Start["App operation"] --> Cloud{"external Supabase reachable?"}
  Cloud -->|No, before sign-in| AuthBlocked["Protected pages unavailable, redirected to /"]
  Cloud -->|Session already valid| LocalScreens["Local-only screens (school, stats, planner, profile links)<br/>may remain usable"]
  Cloud -->|Yes| Gate["Authentication and chat/thread history available"]
  Gate --> Python{"Local Python backend (default 127.0.0.1:8001) reachable?"}
  Python -->|Yes| AI["Context-backed chat works via POST /api/chat"]
  Python -->|No, or backend error| Error["frontend/src/routes/api/chat.ts preserves structured status, code and request ID<br/>default 503, no fallback answer is generated<br/>CURRENT - INTEGRATED"]
  Python -. future health UI .-> Banner["Non-blocking offline banner + Retry<br/>DEFERRED / frontend not wired"]
  Banner -.-> Disable["Disable AI-only actions<br/>PLANNED"]
  Error --> Continue["School, grades, stats, planner, profile and links remain usable locally"]
  Disable --> Continue
  Continue --> Store["Browser storage (AppDataProvider)"]
  ModelDown{"Local model runtime down but FastAPI reachable"} --> Degraded["GET /health reports degraded and model reachability false<br/>CURRENT - BACKEND"]
  Degraded -. planned UI .-> Banner
